  "modules": [
    {
      "title": "Module 1 \u00b7 Distance and Midpoint",
      "html": "$$\\text{Distance}=\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2}$$$$\\text{Midpoint}=\\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\ \\dfrac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right)$$<h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$d=\\sqrt{(6-3)^2+(2--2)^2} = \\sqrt{25} = 5$.</li><li>$d=\\sqrt{(2--4)^2+(11-3)^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the distance between $(3,-2)$ and $(6,2)$.<br/><b>A:</b> 5</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the distance between $(-4,3)$ and $(2,11)$.<br/><b>A:</b> 10</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>Find the distance between $(3,-2)$ and $(6,2)$. \u2014 5.</li><li>Find the distance between $(-4,3)$ and $(2,11)$. \u2014 10.</li><li>Find the distance between $(5,-3)$ and $(11,5)$. \u2014 10.</li><li>Find the distance between $(5,2)$ and $(17,7)$. \u2014 13.</li></ul>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find the distance between $(1,2)$ and $(4,6)$.",
          "a": "$d=\\sqrt{(4-1)^2+(6-2)^2}=\\sqrt{9+16}=\\sqrt{25}=5$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 2 \u00b7 Gradient, Parallel & Perpendicular",
      "html": "$$m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}$$<p>Parallel lines have <b>equal gradients</b>. Perpendicular lines have gradients whose product is $-1$: $m_1 m_2 = -1$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} = \\dfrac{-3}{1} = -3$.</li><li>$m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} = \\dfrac{2}{4} = 1/2$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the gradient of the line through $(4,3)$ and $(5,0)$.<br/><b>A:</b> -3</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the gradient of the line through $(-2,-2)$ and $(2,0)$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{2}</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(4,3)$ and $(5,0)$. \u2014 -3.</li><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(-2,-2)$ and $(2,0)$. \u2014 \\dfrac{1}{2}.</li><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(5,0)$ and $(11,-10)$. \u2014 \\dfrac{-5}{3}.</li><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(-4,-3)$ and $(2,7)$. \u2014 \\dfrac{5}{3}.</li></ul>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "A line has gradient $2/3$. What is the gradient of any line perpendicular to it?",
          "a": "$-3/2$ (since $\\tfrac{2}{3}\\cdot -\\tfrac{3}{2} = -1$)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 3 \u00b7 Equation of a Line",
      "html": "<p><b>Slope-intercept:</b> $y = mx + c$. <b>Point-slope:</b> $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$. <b>General:</b> $Ax + By + C = 0$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} = \\dfrac{-3}{1} = -3$.</li><li>$m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} = \\dfrac{2}{4} = 1/2$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the gradient of the line through $(4,3)$ and $(5,0)$.<br/><b>A:</b> -3</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the gradient of the line through $(-2,-2)$ and $(2,0)$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{2}</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(4,3)$ and $(5,0)$. \u2014 -3.</li><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(-2,-2)$ and $(2,0)$. \u2014 \\dfrac{1}{2}.</li><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(5,0)$ and $(11,-10)$. \u2014 \\dfrac{-5}{3}.</li><li>Find the gradient of the line through $(-4,-3)$ and $(2,7)$. \u2014 \\dfrac{5}{3}.</li></ul>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find the equation of the line through $(2,3)$ with slope $4$.",
          "a": "$y - 3 = 4(x - 2) \\Rightarrow y = 4x - 5$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Revision and exam focus",
      "html": "<p>Revise the whole topic by working through its key points in order, then test yourself with the 50-question quiz for this topic. Pay attention to definitions, differences between similar terms, and questions that ask you to apply the topic rather than only recall it.</p><h4>Worked examples</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the distance between $(3,-2)$ and $(6,2)$.<br/><b>A:</b> 5 \u2014 $d=\\sqrt{(6-3)^2+(2--2)^2} = \\sqrt{25} = 5$.</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the distance between $(-4,3)$ and $(2,11)$.<br/><b>A:</b> 10 \u2014 $d=\\sqrt{(2--4)^2+(11-3)^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$.</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the distance between $(5,-3)$ and $(11,5)$.<br/><b>A:</b> 10 \u2014 $d=\\sqrt{(11-5)^2+(5--3)^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$.</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find the distance between $(3,-2)$ and $(6,2)$.",
          "a": "5"
        },
        {
          "q": "Find the distance between $(-4,3)$ and $(2,11)$.",
          "a": "10"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Key definitions",
      "html": "<p>Learn these definitions exactly as stated \u2014 they are the terms examiners use.</p><ul><li><b>Point-slope:</b>: $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$</li><li><b>General:</b>: $Ax + By + C = 0$</li></ul>",
      "examples": []
    }
  ],
